A small and simple nodejs server that purely reads statistics out of a mysql server.
It writes nothing — only SHOW GLOBAL STATUS, SHOW GLOBAL VARIABLES and information_schema.
It polls at configurable intervals and keeps the previous sample so counters are shown as per second rates.
It serves a page with connections, throughput, query mix, innodb, per database sizes and the live processlist.
Its own polling connections are filtered out of the counts and the processlist, shown in the ui as -4.
Starting the stats page is also configurable — with it off it just polls and logs.
its a very small number of lines.
We only use pnpm.
